WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.533
The battle

00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:01.201
for eastern

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.902
Ukraine was incredibly intense

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:03.870
and bloody this week

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:04.571
as Russia

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.672
hammered its neighbor

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.707
with all manner of munitions

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.341
in Bermuda,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.210
the most hotly contested city

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.211
in the region.

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.445
Wagner mercenaries

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:14.314
fighting on behalf of Moscow

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:15.448
raised the Wagner,

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:16.082
not Russian

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:18.084
flag near the center of the city.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.186
Where does the war go from here?

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:21.955
Let me bring in my guest today,

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.123
retired Admiral

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:24.257
William McRaven

00:00:24.257 --> 00:00:25.258
before he retired

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.293
from the military in 2014.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:29.662
McRaven led special operations command

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:30.930
where he oversaw

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.766
the US military's most elite

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:34.100
combat units.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:34.834
McRaven has

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:36.736
another terrific new book

00:00:36.736 --> 00:00:37.370
is called

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.140
The Wisdom of the Bullfrog Leadership

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.375
Made Simple but Not Easy.

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:44.210
Bill, welcome.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.179
Thanks for a good to be with you.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:49.082
When you look at this Bakhmut situation,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:50.984
Zelinsky had to make

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.118
a very important decision

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.187
which was whether to hold the line here.

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:56.790
It will a lot of people to say militarily

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.058
this is not significant.

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:00.160
Why devote so much space?

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:00.860
He did it

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.929
and he seems to have so far resisted

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.397
the Russian advance.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:05.498
Was it worth it

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.401
or was this a lot of Ukrainian manpower

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:10.470
sacrificed for nothing?

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.404
Yeah,
I actually think

00:01:11.404 --> 00:01:12.572
it was the right decision.

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.074
And again, tactically, when you

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.809
when you look at it militarily,

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:16.676
as you know, about a month

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.577
ago, his advisers

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:17.944
said, look,

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.312
we need to do an orderly withdrawal

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:19.913
from Baltimore

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:21.181
because it's just not worth

00:01:21.181 --> 00:01:24.117
the cost of the soldiers we're losing.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.718
But I think what Zelenskiy

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:26.553
looked at was, look,

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:27.320
if we lose

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.956
Bermuda, plays into Putin's narrative

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.358
that the Russians are winning.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.326
And oh, by the way,

00:01:33.326 --> 00:01:34.994
it will you know, it will bolster

00:01:34.994 --> 00:01:35.795
Russian morale.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.497
It will probably unduly affect

00:01:37.497 --> 00:01:38.465
Ukrainian morale.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:41.234
It could also affect support from Europe

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.469
and the United States.

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:43.403
So while it is

00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:45.371
just a small tactical piece of ground,

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:46.139
I think it has huge

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:47.474
strategic implications.

00:01:47.474 --> 00:01:48.775
I think Zelensky understood this

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.477
and I think was the right call.

00:01:50.477 --> 00:01:52.946
How does Ukraine win against an enemy

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:54.814
that, in the end of the day

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.217
is sort of many, many times bigger

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.886
The defense budget is ten times bigger.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:01.387
The number of people

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:03.623
Putin can call in are so much larger.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.759
So I think winning looks like ensuring

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:08.795
that Russia doesn't achieve its goals.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:10.296
So when when the invasion

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.197
first started, of course,

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:12.165
there were these.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:12.899
I mean, Putin's narrative

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:13.867
was, we're going to take Kiev,

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.068
we're going to come in through hockey.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.503
You've come up through

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.204
Crimea, come in through the Donbass,

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:20.206
and we will essentially take Ukraine.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.908
Well, when that didn't work so well,

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.810
then he moved the goalposts.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:24.577
And that was about,

00:02:24.577 --> 00:02:25.745
well, we're going to build a land bridge

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.014
from Donbass down to Crimea.

00:02:28.014 --> 00:02:30.383
And now he is struggling to do that.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.253
So if the Ukrainians can prevent

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:34.787
the Russians

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.856
from actually building that land bridge

00:02:36.856 --> 00:02:38.258
then I think what it does

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:40.193
is it forces Putin once again

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.361
to move the goalposts.

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:43.163
And frankly, sooner or later,

00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.998
failure is going to be on the radar

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.666
for everybody that's watching this

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.801
so they don't have to take back the dawn,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.236
but they don't have to take back Crimea.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.504
I know they'd like to.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.039
What they've got to do is prevent

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:53.673
the Russians

00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:55.208
from building that land bridge.

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:57.143
And I do think they can do that.

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:58.511
And do you think the key for

00:02:58.511 --> 00:02:58.978
the West

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.580
is just give them all the weapons

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:01.247
they can get?

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:01.881
Yeah, I'm

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:02.315
a believer

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:03.550
that we need to give them

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:05.852
whatever it takes to win the war,

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.319
whatever it takes

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.487
for them to be successful.

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.088
Now, there's been a lot of discussion

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.757
about, you know, do we,

00:03:10.757 --> 00:03:11.291
you know,

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:12.258
help with the Europeans

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:13.359
and give them MiG 29

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.195
or do we give them attack them

00:03:15.195 --> 00:03:16.796
for their high Mars?

00:03:16.796 --> 00:03:19.365
You know, I trust General Mark Milley,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:20.433
one of the finest officers

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.201
I ever served with,

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:22.869
and obviously Secretary Lloyd Austin.

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.837
Both of these gentlemen have incredible

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.272
combat experience.

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.541
So if they are kind of withholding

00:03:28.942 --> 00:03:29.876
the aircraft

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.110
and withholding the attack arms,

00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:32.412
I got to believe there's a good reason

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:33.213
for that.

00:03:33.213 --> 00:03:34.380
But I think in general,

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.081
the administration

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:37.250
has kind of managed the war pretty well.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.519
Now, what they've got to do is decide

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.187
whether or not they want to win the war,

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:42.822
and that being the Ukrainians

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.057
helping the Ukrainians win the war.

